<title>LUXEMBOURG: Dutch back reduction in EU grain storage payments.</title>
<headline>Dutch back reduction in EU grain storage payments.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch EU Presidency, in a compromise on 1997/98 (July/June) farm prices, on Tuesday kept a proposal for a nine percent cut to 1.0 Ecus a tonne in monthly increases for grain held in intervention stores.</p>
<p>The European Commission had proposed the reduction in view of lower interest rates and storage costs.</p>
<p>Cereals intervention prices are raised each month between November and end-May to take account of storage costs and to discourage farmers and merchants from selling into intervention stores at the earliest opportunity.</p>
<p>Southern member states and Sweden have a slightly different schedule.</p>
</text>
